('127.415.d.15.C',3,'A project team in which members trust one another and share information openly will likely have:','["random outcomes", "worse outcomes", "better project outcomes", "no outcomes"]'::jsonb,2,'Healthy dynamics help results.','original'),
('127.415.d.15.C',4,'Unresolved conflict within a team can lower member motivation and:','["parking", "lunch quality", "weather", "project quality"]'::jsonb,3,'Team dynamics affect quality.','original'),
('127.415.d.16.A',3,'Engineering codes of ethics from professional societies place priority on protecting the:','["public''s health, safety, and welfare", "engineer''s comfort", "client''s schedule", "firm''s profit"]'::jsonb,0,'Public safety comes first.','original'),
('127.415.d.16.A',4,'An engineer asked to approve work that violates safety codes should refuse because the code of ethics requires:','["secrecy", "public safety over client wishes", "speed over safety", "profit over safety"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics prioritize safety.','original'),
('127.415.d.16.B',3,'Studying the causes of a historical bridge collapse helps engineers by revealing the:','["weather only", "names of the workers only", "root causes that led to failure", "price of materials only"]'::jsonb,2,'Case studies reveal lessons.','original'),
('127.415.d.16.B',4,'Lessons learned from past failures are typically written into updated:','["calendars", "menus", "jokes", "codes and standards"]'::jsonb,3,'Failures drive improvement of standards.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.A',3,'Using recycled materials in construction can reduce environmental impact but may change the project''s:','["cost or performance", "mascot", "name", "color only"]'::jsonb,0,'Sustainable choices involve trade-offs.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.A',4,'Green building practices can lower long-term operating costs by reducing a building''s:','["height", "energy and water use", "color", "age"]'::jsonb,1,'Efficiency saves money over time.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.B',3,'A cost-benefit analysis of solar panels on a school compares the installation cost to the savings on:','["furniture", "paint", "electricity bills", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Savings are the benefit.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.B',4,'If panels cost 100,000 dollars and save 10,000 dollars per year, the simple payback period is:','["1,000 years", "100 years", "1 year", "10 years"]'::jsonb,3,'100,000 / 10,000 = 10.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.C',3,'At the federal level, a major agency that regulates environmental impact is the:','["Environmental Protection Agency", "Postal Service", "Census Bureau", "Weather Service"]'::jsonb,0,'The EPA regulates pollution.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.C',4,'At the state level in Texas, environmental regulations are administered by the Texas Commission on:','["Elections", "Environmental Quality", "Entertainment", "Education"]'::jsonb,1,'TCEQ regulates environmental matters.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.D',3,'Construction can harm the natural world by causing erosion, habitat loss, and:','["shade", "quiet", "water pollution", "good weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Construction has environmental impacts.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.D',4,'Disturbing soil on a construction site can send sediment into streams, harming:','["office staff", "tourism only", "traffic", "aquatic life"]'::jsonb,3,'Sediment is a pollutant.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.E',3,'Silt fences and sediment basins are methods engineers use to:','["reduce erosion and runoff", "increase erosion", "hide soil", "increase noise"]'::jsonb,0,'These controls mitigate impacts.','original'),
('127.415.d.17.E',4,'Cleaning up contaminated soil at a former industrial site is an example of environmental:','["demolition", "remediation", "advertising", "landscaping only"]'::jsonb,1,'Remediation removes contamination.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.A',3,'To size a water treatment plant for the future, engineers use population projections based on past:','["fashions", "weather", "growth trends", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Projections guide design capacity.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.A',4,'A town of 10,000 grows at 2 percent per year. After one year it will have about:','["10,020 people", "12,000 people", "9,800 people", "10,200 people"]'::jsonb,3,'10,000 x 1.02 = 10,200.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.B',3,'Water quality standards commonly give contaminant limits in milligrams per:','["liter", "degree", "mile", "hour"]'::jsonb,0,'mg/L is a standard unit.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.B',4,'A drinking water limit of 10 mg/L means no more than 10 milligrams of a substance in each:','["gallon of air", "liter of water", "kilogram of soil", "hour of flow"]'::jsonb,1,'Concentration is mass per volume.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.C',3,'Regulations for water supply design specify minimum requirements for the water quantity and:','["scent", "color", "pressure", "taste only"]'::jsonb,2,'Design codes list minimums.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.C',4,'A water system must be sized to meet peak demand, not just the average, because use is highest at certain:','["colors", "names", "seasons only", "times of day"]'::jsonb,3,'Peak demand drives capacity.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.D',3,'Wastewater design rules specify minimum capacity based on the expected flow from a:','["community''s population", "weather", "traffic", "school mascot"]'::jsonb,0,'Flow estimates drive size.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.D',4,'Sewers must be designed with enough slope so that wastewater keeps flowing at a speed that prevents:','["pipes from existing", "solids from settling", "tourists", "rain"]'::jsonb,1,'Self-cleansing velocity prevents clogs.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.E',3,'Wastewater treatment commonly removes solids by letting them settle in a:','["garage", "kitchen", "clarifier", "greenhouse"]'::jsonb,2,'Clarifiers allow settling.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.E',4,'Chlorine or ultraviolet light is often used at the end of water treatment to:','["add sound", "add taste", "add color", "disinfect the water"]'::jsonb,3,'Disinfection kills pathogens.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.F',3,'Solid waste is often managed by burying it in a:','["sanitary landfill", "swimming pool", "parking lot", "greenhouse"]'::jsonb,0,'Landfills are engineered sites.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.F',4,'Recycling reduces the amount of solid waste sent to landfills and conserves:','["time only", "natural resources", "space on shelves", "money only"]'::jsonb,1,'Recycling saves resources.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.G',3,'Hazardous waste must be handled with controls that prevent it from:','["being visible", "being named", "contaminating the environment", "being counted"]'::jsonb,2,'Containment protects people and nature.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.G',4,'A double-lined landfill with leachate collection is used to prevent harmful liquids from reaching:','["rooftops", "sidewalks", "playgrounds", "groundwater"]'::jsonb,3,'Liners protect groundwater.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.H',3,'Air quality is commonly measured using monitors that detect pollutants such as ozone and:','["particulate matter", "water", "sunlight", "music"]'::jsonb,0,'Particulates are monitored.','original'),
('127.415.d.18.H',4,'Reducing vehicle emissions and industrial discharges are two ways to manage:','["water pressure", "air quality", "traffic signs", "building height"]'::jsonb,1,'Source control improves air.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
